\section{Design flow}
A pandas table is also queried cell by cell: for $T = 100$ years, the
rainfall is \py{f"{quantiles.loc[100, 'P']:.1f}"}~mm. With a time of
concentration of \py{f"{t_c:.2f}"}~h (from the file \texttt{station\_data.py}), the
design intensity for $T = 100$ years is \py{f"{intensity(100, t_c * 60):.1f}"}~mm/h,
and for $T = 500$ years, \py{f"{intensity(500, t_c * 60):.1f}"}~mm/h.

\pyif{station["catchment"] > 15}{The catchment, of \py{station["catchment"]}~km$^2$, is medium-sized: the result should be checked against a hydrological model.}{The catchment is small: the rational method is enough.}
